/*
 * Declares the MapLenAccessValue class.
 *
 * MapLenAccessValue represents a pseudo-field access on a map value that
 * returns the number of elements stored in the map. Although it uses the same
 * syntactic form as a field access (`map.len`), it is not a real field access:
 * retrieving the length requires a runtime call to the map’s length function.
 *
 * The result is never an lvalue, and the operation inherits throwers from the
 * map operand.

 *
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::fields::map
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/fields/map.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-03-02
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
